# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. They are authored on Windows but executed
# on the Linux VPS, and a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# literally named "/bin/bash\r" — which fails as "bad interpreter: No such file
# or directory". Pin them so a future clone or editor cannot reintroduce CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
